# Google Drive at ~/GoogleDrive via rclone (remote "gdrive", set up once with
# `rclone config`; its token lives in ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf, never in this
# repo). Full VFS cache so apps can open and save files normally.
# Enable (no sudo):  systemctl --user enable --now rclone-gdrive.service
# Status:            systemctl --user status rclone-gdrive   ·   ls ~/GoogleDrive
[Unit]
Description=Google Drive (rclone mount at ~/GoogleDrive)
Documentation=man:rclone(1)
After=default.target

[Service]
Type=notify
ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/mkdir -p %h/GoogleDrive %h/.cache/rclone
ExecStart=/usr/bin/rclone mount gdrive: %h/GoogleDrive \
    --vfs-cache-mode full \
    --vfs-cache-max-size 10G \
    --vfs-cache-max-age 72h \
    --dir-cache-time 30m \
    --poll-interval 1m \
    --cache-dir %h/.cache/rclone \
    --log-level NOTICE
# Clean unmount on logout / stop (lazy, so an open file doesn't block it)
ExecStop=/usr/bin/fusermount3 -uz %h/GoogleDrive
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=15

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
